From: Ted Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:30:54 -0700
Subject: Add workaround for AV1 Issue in old iHD drivers

This will disable AV1 HW decode for ~9% of all linux users in the last
28 days according to UMA. This number represents 16% of all linux/intel
users, and 21% of all linux/intel/iHD users.

Fixed: 556576976
Change-Id: I65d6137bea6e8233d45c5ca450070d4736bb962a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8384191
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1696620}

diff --git a/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json b/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
index d62036543c0d80d3f33248f95c83e45a5412f972..ca05a81d69f3826ced82810da95e152e6509535e 100644
--- a/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
